11	// Regression coverage for the relationship between whole-batch ingestion
12	// (POST /events) and alert previews (POST /alerts/preview): every preview
13	// response must be computed from one committed snapshot. The groups, window
14	// counts, end-of-window statuses, and alert trigger/recovery times must all
15	// belong to the same observation, never a mix of two batches.
16	//
17	// The discriminating scenario: one-minute windows, threshold 2, trigger on
18	// two consecutive windows at/over the threshold, recover on one window below
19	// it. The seeded "old" label group has counts [2,1,0] (no alert); one batch
20	// tops its middle window up to 2 while filling a second label group "new"
21	// with [2,2,0]. After the commit both groups alert at the end of window 1 and
22	// recover at the end of the empty window 2. A partial application of the
23	// batch would surface as a group or a state machine that matches neither the
24	// committed-before nor the committed-after result.
